<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0335">Definition <span data-tag="0335">4.5.3.8</span>.</a> A commutative diagram of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation" id="0336">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="0336" href="/tag/0336">4.23</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:categorical-pullback-square} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{01} \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1 \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}. } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> is a <em>categorical pullback square</em> if the composite map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{01} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{1} \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{0} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\mathrm{h}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1 \]
</div>
<p> is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. </p>
